<title>USA: Reebok CFO downplays future share buybacks.</title>
<headline>Reebok CFO downplays future share buybacks.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reebok International Ltd Chief Financial Officer Ken Watchmaker said the company is authorized to spend about $130 million on share repurchases, but instead will likely conserve cash.</p>
<p>&quot;Don't expect us to be making open market share repurchases in the near term,&quot; Watchmaker told analysts and reporters during a conference call.</p>
<p>Reebok completed a &quot;Dutch auction&quot; buyback of more than 17 million shares in late August and since 1991 has spent more than $1.7 billion in buying 62.3 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Michael Ellis, Boston bureau (617) 367-4176</p>
</text>
